What Is Correct
✅ Architecture Flow
The forward and rollback flows described in the document are consistent with the implementation you shared:

listener.py → file_events
batch_creator.py → sync_batches
worker.py → rclone
rollback_listener.py → blob_events
rollback_batch_creator.py → rollback_batches
rollback_worker.py → rclone
✅ PostgreSQL as Source of Truth
The document correctly treats PostgreSQL as the operational state store rather than Pub/Sub or Azure Queue. Your code confirms workers process batches from PostgreSQL tables.

✅ Partitioning Recommendation
Monthly partitioning of file_events and blob_events is a good future-state recommendation for very large volumes.

✅ Retention Strategy
90-day retention plus periodic archival is reasonable for event-processing tables.

✅ Daily Monitoring
The health checks, queue monitoring, worker monitoring, and status queries are useful operational procedures.

